  "goodToKnow": "Die Dividende is a dividend: eine Dividende ausschütten (to pay out), die Dividende kürzen or streichen. German companies usually pay dividends once a year after the Hauptversammlung (AGM) approves them, unlike quarterly US payouts. Dividends are subject to Abgeltungsteuer (flat-rate capital gains tax) of 25 percent plus solidarity surcharge. Germans traditionally invest less in shares than Americans. Plural: die Dividenden."
